# Everything the Go build doesn't need. Without this the build context pulled
# in node_modules and Vale's style packages — tens of megabytes docker has to
# hash and send to the daemon before the first instruction even runs.
#
# node_modules/ (bare, no leading **/) only matches at the context root — it
# does NOT also match web/node_modules, unlike a .gitignore pattern of the
# same shape. Left that way once, COPY web/ web/ in the web-build stage
# still pulled in a locally-installed web/node_modules -- bun hoists
# packages there as symlinks into the repo root's own node_modules/.bun
# store, which the web-build stage never copies, so every symlink dangled
# once inside the container and silently overwrote the fresh, working
# node_modules RUN bun install had just produced. Never reproduced in CI
# (a fresh checkout has no local node_modules to begin with to collide),
# only on a dev machine that already ran bun install -- which is the
# ordinary local workflow, so this broke `docker build` under the
# pre-push hook specifically, the one place it's most likely to be hit.
.git/
.github/
**/node_modules/
.bun-cache/
styles/Google/
styles/proselint/
dist/
coverage.out
*.md
web/.svelte-kit/
web/build/
